  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Prakash Premaramji Bhati vs The State Of Maharashtra on 19 October, 2023 Author: N.J.Jamadar Bench: N.J.Jamadar 913 aba 2926 of 2023. IN THE HIGH COURT OF JUDICATURE AT BOMBAY CRIMINAL APPELLATE JURISDICTION ANTICIPATORY BAIL APPLICATION NO.2926 OF 2023 Prakash Premaramji Bhati ... Applicant versus The State of Maharashtra ... Respondent Mr. Ganesh Gupta with Mr. Rahul Lolandkar, Mr. Sahil Ghorpade, for Applicant. Mr. M.G.Patil, APP for State. CORAM: N.J.JAMADAR, J. DATE : 19 OCTOBER 2023 P.C. 2. This is an application for pre-arrest bail in connection with CR No.508 of 2022, registered with Yerwada Police Station, for the offences punishable under Sections 328, 188, 272 and 273 read with Section 34 of Indian Penal Code, 1860 (\"the Penal Code\") and Sections 26(2)(i), (iv) 27(3)(d), 3(1)(zz)(iv) and 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006.",
    "facts": "2. This is an application for pre-arrest bail in connection with CR No.508 of 2022, registered with Yerwada Police Station, for the offences punishable under Sections 328, 188, 272 and 273 read with Section 34 of Indian Penal Code, 1860 (\"the Penal Code\") and Sections 26(2)(i), (iv) 27(3)(d), 3(1)(zz)(iv) and 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. 2. This is an application seeking pre-arrest bail in connection with C.R No. 508 of 2022 registered with Yerwada Police Station for offence punishable under Section 328, 188, 272, 273 read with Section 34 of IPC and Section 26(2)(i), (iv), 27(3)(d), 3(1)(zz)(iv) and 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. 3. The Applicant was protected by interim order of this Court on 19.10.2023. 4. It was pointed out on the last occasion that after interim protection was granted in this application, one more FIR is filed bearing No. 1171 of 2023 with Kondhwa Police Station for same offence against the Applicant, who is accused No.2 in said FIR No. 1171 of 2023. Other earlier FIRs were also pointed out. Perusal of the allegations in present FIR and the subsequent FIR No. 1171 of 2023 indicates that the allegations are identical inasmuch as the vehicle carrying contraband material (Gutkha Pan Masala etc.), the driver of the vehicle has named the present Applicant as a person for whom the contraband was being carried or on whose instance the said contraband is stated to be carried.",
    "arguments": "6. Today, learned Counsel for the Applicant submits that in 3 earlier FIRs namely 948/2020, 1143/2020 and 795/2022, the Applicant has been acquitted. He submits that the application of Section 328 of IPC to Gutkha is pending before the Hon'ble Supreme Court and submits that on this count alone, the anticipatory bail application be allowed. 8. Learned APP on instructions of concerned Investigating Officer (who is present in the Court) has strenuously opposed this application on the ground that considering various FIRs, the Applicant is a habitual offender and is a supplier of the contraband material involved in the FIR.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "6. Today, learned Counsel for the Applicant submits that in 3 earlier FIRs namely 948/2020, 1143/2020 and 795/2022, the Applicant has been acquitted. He submits that the application of Section 328 of IPC to Gutkha is pending before the Hon'ble Supreme Court and submits that on this count alone, the anticipatory bail application be allowed. 8. Learned APP on instructions of concerned Investigating Officer (who is present in the Court) has strenuously opposed this application on the ground that considering various FIRs, the Applicant is a habitual offender and is a supplier of the contraband material involved in the FIR.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
